{{Commonscat|Begonia grandis}}

'''''Begonia grandis''''', the '''hardy begonia''',<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref><ref name=Missouri>[http://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/gardens-gardening/your-garden/plant-finder/plant-details/kc/c843/begonia-grandis.aspx Missouri Botanical Garden: ''Begonia grandis'']</ref> is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the [[family (botany)|family]] [[Begoniaceae]]. This [[herbaceous]] [[perennial plant|perennial]] has alternate, simple leaves on arching stems. The flowers are pink or white, borne in [[dichotomous branching|dichotomously]] branching [[Cyme (botany)|cymes]] from late summer through fall in [[USDA hardiness zone|USDA U.S. Hardiness Zone]] 7. As the common name "hardy begonia" implies, it is winter [[hardiness (plants)|hardy]] in some temperate regions.

It can overwinter well in hardiness zone 9a in southwestern Japan as tuberous roots or bulbils (bulbils are formed in axils). Above-ground parts of this plant eventually die as temperature lowers. However, it is generally regarded as hardy to zones 5-6.
<ref name=Missouri/><ref>[http://www.pfaf.org/user/Plant.aspx?LatinName=Begonia+grandis Plants for a Future]</ref>

The varietIes ''Begonia grandis'' subsp. ''evansiana''<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/95775/Begonia-grandis-subsp-evansiana/Details | title = ''Begonia grandis'' subsp. ''evansiana'' | publisher = RHS | accessdate = 12 April 2020}}</ref> and ''Begonia grandis'' subsp. ''evansiana'' var. ''alba'' have gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/63105/Begonia-grandis-Dryand-subsp-evansiana-(Andrews)-Irmsch-var-alba-hort/Details | title = ''Begonia grandis'' subsp. ''evansiana'' var. ''alba'' | website = www.rhs.org | publisher = Royal Horticultural Society | accessdate = 12 April 2020}}</ref> 
